## 🎯 Summary & Learnings
In this room, I covered the foundational concepts of the **Metasploit Framework (MSF)**. I gained hands-on experience in initializing the framework, navigating its architecture, executing modules, and leveraging its features for vulnerability exploitation and post-exploitation.

### Key Concepts Covered:
- **MSF Architecture:** Understanding Modules (Exploits, Payloads, Auxiliary, Encoders, Nops, Post).
- **Core Commands:** Navigating `msfconsole`, managing global/local options (`set`, `setg`), and searching for specific exploits.
- **Payload Selection:** Differentiating between Staged (`shell/reverse_tcp`) and Non-staged (`shell_reverse_tcp`) payloads.
- **Session Management:** Backgrounding sessions and managing active Meterpreter sessions.

---

## 🛠️ Essential Commands Reference

| Action | Command / Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Launch Console** | `msfconsole` |
| **Search Module** | `search <vulnerability / service / CVE>` |
| **Select Module** | `use <module_path>` |
| **View Info** | `info` or `show options` |
| **Set Target/Payload** | `set RHOSTS <IP>` / `set LHOST <IP>` |
| **Execute Exploit** | `exploit` or `run` |
| **Background Session**| `Ctrl + Z` or `background` |
| **List Sessions** | `sessions -l` |
| **Interact Session** | `sessions -i <ID>` |

